class.description:
Returned by [method DataSchema.validate] and [method TextDataFormat.validate]. Each issue has a kind ([enum IssueKind]), a message and its position:
- the field name ([method get_issue_field]),
- the path of keys and indices joined with [code]/[/code] ([method get_issue_path], such as [code]"enemies/3/hp"[/code]; [code]~[/code] and [code]/[/code] in keys are written [code]~0[/code] and [code]~1[/code]),
- the 0-based row (the entry of the root list, or the CSV data row without the header) and the 0-based CSV column,
- the 1-based line in the text, only with [member DataValidationOptions.keep_positions] or after [method resolve_lines].
Positions that do not apply are [constant POSITION_NONE].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var result = schema.validate(data)
if not result.is_valid():
	for i in result.get_issue_count():
		if result.get_issue_kind(i) == DataValidation.ISSUE_KIND_MISSING_FIELD:
			print("Missing: ", result.get_issue_field(i))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
DataValidation result = schema.Validate(data);
if (!result.IsValid())
{
	for (int i = 0; i < result.GetIssueCount(); i++)
	{
		if (result.GetIssueKind(i) == DataValidation.IssueKind.MissingField)
		{
			GD.Print("Missing: ", result.GetIssueField(i));
		}
	}
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
Own checks can add issues with [method add_issue], so one result type serves all checks of a file.
